              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for the horizon, then the Hindi for dusk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शिखर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिखर — śikhar — \"a peak, a summit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हम सुबह तक पहाड़ के शिखर पर पहुँचे। ham subah tak pahāṛ ke śikhar par pahũce. We reached the top of the mountain by morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिखर (śikhar) is a tatsama, Sanskrit śikhara, \"pointed, crested\" and so a peak (Monier-Williams); the spire of a temple is its शिखर too."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
